# Copy to .env (git-ignored) for local use. NEVER commit real values.
# In production DATABASE_URL lives in Vercel project settings (exact name, capital letters, case-sensitive);
# DATABASE_URL_MIGRATE only on your PC / CI.
#
# BEST: do not type these. In Supabase click Connect, copy the "Transaction pooler" string, copy the
# "Session pooler" string, and replace ONLY the word PASTE_PASSWORD_HERE with your password.
# Common mistakes (the app tells you which one at /api/db_ping): leaving a placeholder such as <n> or
# [YOUR-PASSWORD] in the string, wrapping the value in quotes, or a password containing # / ? @ without URL-encoding.

# Transaction pooler (port 6543), used by the Rust functions:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASTE_PASSWORD_HERE@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require

# Session pooler (port 5432), used only by `npm run migrate`:
DATABASE_URL_MIGRATE=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASTE_PASSWORD_HERE@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# Your time zone (IANA name such as Europe/Paris or America/New_York): what "today" means for the News tab's
# Today card and the "no briefing" check. Set it in Vercel too. Default UTC.
#LIFEUI_TIMEZONE=UTC
